                "reply_count": 11,
                "retweet_count": 5,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "My statement on the Biden-Harris administration\u2019s plan to artificially set prescription drug prices:\n\nWhen it comes to health care, we need patient-focused solutions, lower prices, and more cures; however, under the Biden-Harris administration\u2019s so-called \u2018Inflation Reduction Act\u2019 \u2013 which imposes an artificial drug pricing scheme \u2013 patients will experience the exact opposite.\n\nI agree that we should be finding solutions to help drive down the cost of health care in this country, but it should not come at the expense of American medicinal research and innovation. \n\nThe @HouseCommerce Committee will continue pushing back on this administration\u2019s misguided policies, and we will work toward solutions that put patients and their needs first without impeding their access to critical drugs and cures.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
